// Test 3: rank 5 — two independent stick splits on one operand.
//   A[B=2,M=128,K=128] split on M(64) and K(64)
//     -> phys [M/64, K/64, B, M%64, K%64] = [2, 2, 2, 64, 64]
//   B[B=2,K=128,N=64]  split on K(64) only
//     -> phys [K/64, B, K%64, N] = [2, 2, 64, 64]
// M is parallel (outer scatter loop, trip 2) and K is the reduction (inner
// stick loop, trip 2). This is the case that proves the two IVs are threaded
// independently: A's rank-5 extract_slice indexes the M floor dim with the
// OUTER IV and the K floor dim with the INNER IV, while B's rank-4
// extract_slice sees only the inner IV. Both operands are annotated, so the
// shared-contraction-axis check is satisfied.
module {
// CHECK-LABEL:   tt.func @parallel_floor_rank5(
// CHECK-SAME:  %[[VAL_0:.*]]: !tt.ptr<f16>, %[[VAL_1:.*]]: !tt.ptr<f16>, %[[VAL_2:.*]]: !tt.ptr<f16>) {
// CHECK:           %[[VAL_3:.*]] = arith.constant 0 : i32
// CHECK:           %[[VAL_4:.*]] = builtin.unrealized_conversion_cast %[[VAL_0]] : !tt.ptr<f16> to index
// CHECK:           %[[VAL_5:.*]] = ktdp.construct_memory_view %[[VAL_4]], sizes: [2, 2, 2, 64, 64], strides: [16384, 8192, 4096, 64, 1] {coordinate_set = #[[$ATTR_12]], memory_space = #ktdp.memory_space<global>} : memref<2x2x2x64x64xf16>
// CHECK:           %[[VAL_6:.*]] = arith.index_cast %[[VAL_3]] : i32 to index
// CHECK:           %[[VAL_7:.*]] = arith.index_cast %[[VAL_3]] : i32 to index
// CHECK:           %[[VAL_8:.*]] = arith.index_cast %[[VAL_3]] : i32 to index
